  "unreadable": [
    "O and 0 look alike in the diagram font. The IO/GPIO prefixes are letters, and the digit after them is recorded as 0 (e.g. GPIO0_A0_u, RM_IO0)."
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    "Start end is unclear. The image shows a top-edge connector silkscreened 'USB', but also a USB-C connector at mid-left ('USB') and one near the bottom ('PWR & OTG'). Positions start at the top. If the bottom USB-C is the reference, the order reverses."
  ],
  "notes": "Each pin also carries a '3.3V' voltage tag in the diagram, recorded as a function. The legend says RM_IOs share multiplexed function signals (UART, CAN, SPI, PWM, PMU, I2S, PDM, I2C, SPDIF, TOUCH_KEY); these are not per-pin and are omitted."
